message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Occult hybrid mode switches and barrier-augmented metastatic edge-rate identifiability"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  When occult hybrid mode switches and edge-wise desmoplastic conductances
  coexist on one anatomical graph toy, which metastatic edge rates stay
  practically identifiable from site-plus-barrier schedules that only see a
  mode-blind or mode-partial map? On a three-node, two-edge toy, site burdens
  alone leave all six log-parameters at structural rank 4, and every shedding
  rate has an unbounded marginal variance. A duration-weighted stall on each
  edge restores local practical rank 6. The shedding-limited active rate has
  both neighbouring coarse-grid profile samples outside a chi-squared cut on
  that blind schedule. The transport-limited active rate keeps multipliers
  0.78 through 1.40 inside the cut until its own stall is recorded in both
  modes, which shortens the inside set to 0.86 through 1.16. A continuous-flow
  alias of the blind record is practical rank 4 of 4 and coincides with
  neither hybrid shedding rate. No number is taken from the results files of
  Thesis #20 or Thesis #21. Not a medical device. No document DOI.
keywords:
  - hybrid modes
  - desmoplastic conductance
  - metastatic edge rate
  - practical identifiability
  - profile likelihood
  - mode-blind schedule
  - anatomical graph
  - research-only
